## Instructor grading notes

- Accept any valid 32-character hexadecimal Trace ID captured from the participant's own Jaeger trace URL.
- The same ID must appear in the Jaeger URL and in the Loki LogQL query; the log line should show that ID when queried.
- Do not require the participant's ID to equal the seeded example `4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736`.
- Accept a duration close to 430 ms; timing varies with host load.
- The participant must distinguish inventory HTTP 409 from the outer checkout HTTP 500.
- The safe operational recommendation is to coordinate with warehouse operations, release the bin after the cycle-count audit is complete, and add an explicit conflict/retry or alternate-bin handling path. Do not tell learners to disable audit controls or modify real inventory.
